The semantics supports a bridge-free route: fixed semantics can execute the real function body using `len`, constant string indexing, `ord`, integer arithmetic, Boolean short-circuiting, `if`, and `return`. I’m choosing that route so `verification.k` needs only a mathematical result summary—no rewrite that skips function lookup, body execution, frames, or control flow.
