The first proof attempt exposed a fixed-semantics definedness issue, not a missing calendar fact: from an opaque symbolic `IntSeq`, `isLen(CS) == 10` does not let K prove each `intSeqAt(CS,i)` is defined. I’m repairing this without a bridge by splitting the theorem into the exact ten-constructor case and the complementary non-ten-length case. Together they cover all concrete MPY strings, while every indexed access in the ten-character claim is structurally in bounds.
